<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142d4c"><meta name="description" content="Explore assistance programs available in West Virginia."><title>West Virginia Assistance Programs — American Aid Network</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/site-header.php"; ?><main><section class="state-page"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/help/">Browse Programs</a><span>›</span><b>West Virginia</b></div><div class="state-intro"><div><h1>Assistance Programs in West Virginia</h1><p>10 programs, grouped by what you need help with. Each includes clear application guidance.</p></div><div><a class="button primary" href="/find/">Find my programs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><small>Free · Private · Takes under 2 minutes</small></div></div><section class="program-group"><h2>Utility Bill Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>LIEAP (Low Income Energy Assistance Program)</h3><p>LIEAP helps low-income West Virginia households pay winter heating costs, either as a payment to your utility company or a direct payment. An Emergency LIEAP component helps households without resources facing the loss of a heating source. Apply online through wvPATH at wvpath.wv.gov, at your local Department of Human Services field office, or through a local Community Action agency or Area Agency on Aging.</p><div><a href="/programs/lieap-low-income-energy-assistance-program/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/lieap-low-income-energy-assistance-program/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Weatherization Assistance Program (West Virginia)</h3><p>Free home energy-efficiency work for income-eligible West Virginia households: insulation, air sealing, and heating-system improvements that lower future bills. The work is delivered by local Community Action agencies. Call the West Virginia Community Action Partnership at 304-347-2277 or use its agency locator to reach the weatherization provider serving your county, since you apply through that local agency.</p><div><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-west-virginia/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-west-virginia/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Rent &amp; Housing Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Legal Aid of West Virginia</h3><p>Legal Aid of West Virginia gives free civil legal help to low-income residents on housing and eviction, family law, public benefits, consumer and debt problems, and more. Call the statewide intake line at 1-866-255-4370 to reach the office serving your area, or apply for help online at legalaidwv.org. This is civil, noncriminal help.</p><div><a href="/programs/legal-aid-of-west-virginia/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/legal-aid-of-west-virginia/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>West Virginia 211</h3><p>Dial 2-1-1 from any West Virginia phone, or call 1-833-848-9905, for free, confidential help finding local assistance with housing, utilities, food, healthcare, and more. West Virginia 211 answers 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, every day of the year. You can also text your zip code to 898-211 or search at search.wv211.org.</p><div><a href="/programs/west-virginia-211/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/west-virginia-211/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>West Virginia Medicaid</h3><p>West Virginia Medicaid is free or low-cost health coverage for children, pregnant people, parents, older adults, people with disabilities, and low-income adults. West Virginia expanded Medicaid, so adults 19 to 64 with low income can qualify on their own. Apply online through wvPATH at wvpath.wv.gov, at a local Department of Human Services field office, or by calling the DoHS Customer Service Center at 1-877-716-1212.</p><div><a href="/programs/west-virginia-medicaid/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/west-virginia-medicaid/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Cash Assistance &amp; Benefits</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Unemployment Insurance (WorkForce West Virginia)</h3><p>Temporary weekly payments if you lost work through no fault of your own, from WorkForce West Virginia. File online through the WorkForce West Virginia claims portal at uc.workforcewv.org, which is the fastest way, or get help by phone at 1-800-252-5627 (1-800-252-JOBS). You must file a claim each week to keep payments coming.</p><div><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-workforce-west-virginia/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-workforce-west-virginia/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Free &amp; Low-Cost Healthcare</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>WV CHIP (Children&#39;s Health Insurance Program)</h3><p>WV CHIP covers children and pregnant women in working families who have no other health insurance and earn too much for Medicaid. It covers checkups, dental, vision, prescriptions, and more with low or no cost to the family. Apply through wvPATH along with Medicaid at wvpath.wv.gov, and call the WVCHIP Helpline at 1-877-982-2447 (1-877-WVA-CHIP) with questions.</p><div><a href="/programs/wv-chip-childrens-health-insurance-program/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/wv-chip-childrens-health-insurance-program/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Food Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>WV WORKS (TANF Cash Assistance)</h3><p>WV WORKS is West Virginia&#39;s Temporary Assistance for Needy Families program, giving monthly cash assistance to eligible families with children. It pairs the cash with work and education activities like job skills training, vocational training, and college. Apply online through wvPATH at wvpath.wv.gov or at your local Department of Human Services field office. Most families on WV WORKS also receive SNAP and Medicaid.</p><div><a href="/programs/wv-works-tanf-cash-assistance/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/wv-works-tanf-cash-assistance/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>West Virginia SNAP (Food Assistance)</h3><p>SNAP is West Virginia&#39;s food assistance program: monthly food money on an EBT card you use like a debit card at most grocery stores. Apply online through wvPATH at wvpath.wv.gov, the state&#39;s one application for SNAP, WV WORKS, and Medicaid, at your local Department of Human Services field office, or by phone through the DoHS Customer Service Center at 1-877-716-1212.</p><div><a href="/programs/west-virginia-snap-food-assistance/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/west-virginia-snap-food-assistance/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>West Virginia WIC</h3><p>WIC gives healthy food, breastfeeding support, nutrition education, and health referrals to pregnant and postpartum people, infants, and children up to age 5. West Virginia WIC runs through local clinics tied to county health departments. Check the WIC eligibility screening tool and find your nearest clinic through the state WIC clinic search, then call the clinic to book your first appointment.</p><div><a href="/programs/west-virginia-wic/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/west-virginia-wic/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div></section></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="American Aid Network home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>AMERICAN <b>AID</b><small>NETWORK</small></span></a><p>Clear, reliable guidance to assistance programs across America.</p><div class="verified">✓ Information from trusted sources</div></div><div><h4>FIND SUPPORT</h4><a href="/find/">Find help near me</a><a href="/help/">Browse by state</a><a href="/programs/">Program guides</a><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a></div><div><h4>ABOUT</h4><a href="/about/">Our mission</a><a href="/legal/contact/">Contact us</a><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/legal/terms/">Terms of use</a></div></div><div class="wrap disclaimer">American Aid Network is an independent informational resource. We are not a government agency and do not administer benefit programs. Program details change; always confirm requirements with the official provider.<span>© 2026 American Aid Network</span></div></footer><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></body></html>